The following python code reads the csharp code and outputs assert statements corresponding to the comments that start with "@@@".

```python
def create_assertions(file_name):
    with open(file_name, 'r') as file:
        data = file.readlines()

    assert_lines = [line for line in data if line.strip().startswith('// @@@')]
    for line in assert_lines:
        assert_stmt = line.split('// @@@')[1].strip()
        print(f'Debug.Assert({assert_stmt});')

# example usage 
create_assertions('your_csharp_file.cs')
```

This python script will open a csharp file and search for lines that start with `// @@@`. If found, it will pull out the part of the string after `// @@@` and print it as a Debug.Assert statement in the C# language. Note that, this assumes that your comments are on the same line as the assertions. You may need to update the script to handle multiline comments (blocks of code enclosed in {}), comments at the end of lines, etc. depending on the specifics of your code.--------------------
